  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthening control of ivory trafficking in Cambodia; implementing the National Ivory Action Plan, Phase 2</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project builds upon the work undertaken in USFWS award #F15AP00349, to provide strategic capacity building and technical support to key law enforcement agencies at international trafficking points, to combat trafficking of wildlife, in particular of elephant ivory and rhino horn with the ultimate goal of reducing the trafficking of elephant ivory and rhino horn through Cambodia. Project activities include: 1) conduct training for key law enforcement agencies to intercept and prosecute wildlife trafficking cases at key points in Cambodia; 2) provide technical support to the sampling and inventory of ivory and rhino horns that are seized by law enforcement agencies; 3) establish a secure repository for confiscated wildlife products; and 4) provide technical advice to the national CITES Management Authority. This project will contribute to the strengthening of capacity and awareness within primary law enforcement agencies to combat wildlife trafficking in Cambodia.</narrative>
  </description>
